@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dct:  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix xeo:  <https://xeoontology.org/xeo#> .

# XEO Work module — the container the work happens in. Named xeo-delivery until
# 0.7, when the agency terms it already held (clientOf, holdsCapability, the
# contract fields on Project) made it the home of client work as a whole.
#
# The decision tier says WHAT to do (a Recommendation closes a Gap with a Tactic)
# and the norms tier says what SHOULD govern that call. Neither says for whom,
# under which contract, against which goal, or with how much room left this
# month. That is delivery, and until this module it lived only in the
# implementations: a Project with a quota and a scope, a Campaign against a
# topic with an Objective, and the targets an experiment is finally read against.
#
#   Website hasProject Project                     (the contract: type, quota, scope)
#   Project hasCampaign Campaign                   (a body of work against one Topic)
#   Campaign hasObjective Objective hasTarget MetricTarget   (the intent, as targets)
#   Recommendation issuedFor Campaign              (a call lands in a campaign)
#   Experiment measures MetricTarget               (and is read against its target)
#
# Two layers meet here and are kept apart on purpose. Project and Campaign are
# ENTITIES: they exist because a contract was signed and a topic was chosen.
# Objective and MetricTarget are INTERPRETATIONS: an intent set at creation, a
# call about what should move. A target is named a target and never a result —
# xeo:Outcome is the measured side, an observation, and the two must never share
# a name or the experiment loop will conflate the goal with the reading.
#
# The scope gate now has two halves. xeo-decision's requiresCapability + approved
# asks CAN we (is the lever available); this module's inScope + execution asks
# DID THEY BUY IT and WHOSE HOURS DOES IT COST. A recommendation is deliverable
# when both say yes; advisory when the capability exists but the contract or the
# allowance does not cover it.
#
# Named Project, not Engagement, deliberately: "engagement" was the name of the
# conversion seam (forms, CTAs, the CRM join) until 0.7, and the implementations
# this module is lifted from call the container a Project.
#
# DISCIPLINE (unchanged): classes, never values. engagementType, cadence,
# metric and the rest take their values from xeo-schemes.ttl — published
# reference schemes a consumer adopts or replaces.
#
# NEEDS core only (Website, URL, Term, Topic, Organization, Metric). Its links to
# decision (issuedFor, measures, effortEstimate, execution, holdsCapability,
# inScope) are optional: they work when decision is loaded too. Uses SKOS for its
# slots.

xeo:work-module a owl:Ontology ;
    dct:title "XEO Work (clients, contracts, projects, campaigns, objectives)" ;
    dct:description "The container work is delivered in: a Project (the contract — type, quota, scope), its Campaigns (a body of work against one Topic), the Objective each campaign is measured by, and the MetricTargets an Experiment is read against. Also the agency side: which Organization is whose client, and what it holds. Lifted from a production implementation. Named xeo-delivery until 0.7." ;
    dct:creator "Inbound Found" ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.7.0" .

# --- Classes ----------------------------------------------------------------

xeo:Project a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Project" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "The contractual container for a body of work on one Website. Declares its engagementType (retainer or one-off), an interventionQuota (a scope of work with no ceiling is not a scope), a cadence the quota resets over (retainer) or a durationDays it runs for (one-off), and the Interventions and Tactics inScope under the contract. Never destroyed: its campaigns, objectives and targets are the substrate the end-of-campaign report and the experiment loop read, so it is stamped deletedAt and filtered, not deleted." .

xeo:Campaign a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Campaign" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "A body of work inside a Project against one Topic: the URLs and Terms it covers, and the single Objective it is measured by. Recommendations are issuedFor a campaign, and it is the unit an operator plans a cycle around. Soft-deleted like its Project." .

xeo:Objective a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Objective" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    dct:description "What a Campaign intends to move: an operator-written statement in prose (carried verbatim — the recommendation agent reads it as the goal), a resultsWindowDays every target is measured over, and one or more MetricTargets of which exactly one isPrimary. An intent set at creation. A campaign has one reporting horizon, distinct from the Project's work window: a two-month engagement can carry a six-month results window. The window starts on resultsWindowStart, and the objective-level result is one objectiveReading per target over the campaign's deduplicated scope, never a sum of Outcomes." .

xeo:MetricTarget a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Metric Target" ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    dct:description "One measurable target of an Objective: the Metric it is set on (targetMetric, a link to the Metric node), the targetValue to reach, read per targetKind as an absolute value or as a change from a captured baseline (baselineReading), and whether it isPrimary. Unit and better direction come from its Metric. Named a target and never a key result: xeo:Outcome is 'the measured result an experiment produced', an observation, and a goal must not share a name with a reading. Each target is its own node so the experiment loop can hang observations off it; a target dropped on edit is stamped deletedAt, never destroyed, because its id is what measured history is anchored to." .

# --- Object properties -------------------------------------------------------

xeo:hasProject a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Website ; rdfs:range xeo:Project ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "The projects contracted against this website. Tenancy rides on websiteId, as everywhere." .

xeo:hasCampaign a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Project ; rdfs:range xeo:Campaign ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" .

xeo:inScope a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Project ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "What the contract covers: an Intervention (a whole category of work, including tactics added to the catalogue later) or a specific Tactic within one. Range left open across those two terms. The contractual half of the scope gate — requiresCapability + approved asks whether the lever exists; this asks whether it was bought." .

xeo:aboutTopic a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Campaign ; rdfs:range xeo:Topic ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "The topic cluster this campaign works. Topics are site-scoped derivations in core; a campaign binds to one." .

xeo:coversUrl a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Campaign ; rdfs:range xeo:URL ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "A page inside the campaign's cluster. May carry a priority flag marking the pages the campaign is really about." .

xeo:coversTerm a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Campaign ; rdfs:range xeo:Term ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "A term inside the campaign's cluster — the queries its objective is measured against." .

xeo:hasObjective a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Campaign ; rdfs:range xeo:Objective ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    dct:description "Exactly one per campaign." .

xeo:hasTarget a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Objective ; rdfs:range xeo:MetricTarget ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    dct:description "The objective's measurable targets. Non-empty; exactly one target isPrimary — what the recommendation agent optimises for. The rest are the secondary metrics an impact-radius check widens to." .

xeo:issuedFor a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Recommendation ; rdfs:range xeo:Campaign ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    dct:description "The campaign a recommendation was issued into. Its execution lifecycle (xeo:status), effortEstimate and execution live here: a recommendation is a decision-tier call until it lands in a campaign, and delivery state from then on." .

xeo:measures a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Experiment ; rdfs:range xeo:MetricTarget ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "episode" ;
    dct:description "The target an experiment's Outcome is read against. Carries a role — primary or secondary — matching the target's standing in its objective, and a basis saying which pages were measured (the ones the recommendation applied to, the gap's evidence, or the pages actually changed)." .

xeo:effortEstimate a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Recommendation ; rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    dct:description "How long executing the recommendation is expected to take, as a slotted-in concept (hours, days, weeks, a quarter — see xeo-schemes). A categorical horizon for planning a cycle, not a scored dimension: impact, risk and time-to-value belong on a TacticAssessment via onDimension." .

xeo:execution a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Recommendation ; rdfs:range skos:Concept ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    dct:description "Who does the work, as a slotted-in concept: ours (spends the project's intervention allowance) or advised (the client executes; not agency capacity). The half of the scope gate that says whose hours a recommendation costs." .

# --- Datatype properties -----------------------------------------------------
# xeo:status on a Recommendation is its execution lifecycle (pending, in_progress,
# blocked, cancelled, completed); on an Experiment it is measuring, concluded,
# cancelled, unmeasurable. Both value sets are published in xeo-schemes.ttl. The
# property is declared domain-free in xeo-decision for exactly this reason.

xeo:engagementType a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Project ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "'retainer' or 'oneoff' — the discriminator for how scope is expressed. A retainer caps interventions per cadence period; a one-off caps them over durationDays. Sending both cadence and durationDays is a contradiction and is rejected at the edge." .

xeo:interventionQuota a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Project ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "Ceiling on interventions this project may deploy per period (retainer) or in total (one-off). Always present. Recommendations in an open status — pending, in_progress, blocked — consume it; advised work does not." .

xeo:cadence a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Project ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "'monthly' or 'quarterly' — the period a retainer's quota resets over. Set for retainer, absent for one-off." .

xeo:durationDays a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Project ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "Fixed run length of a one-off project. Set for oneoff, absent for retainer." .

xeo:resultsWindowDays a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Objective ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    dct:description "The measurement window every target in this objective is read over. One horizon per campaign; per-target windows are deliberately not modelled. Counted in days from resultsWindowStart, that day included." .

# Removed in 0.7: xeo:metric. Use targetMetric, which links to the Metric node.




# Removed in 0.7: xeo:direction. Use betterDirection, stated once on the Metric.




xeo:targetKind a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:MetricTarget ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    dct:description "'absolute' (targetValue is a value of the metric) or 'percent' (a relative change from baseline in the metric's better direction). xeos:targetKind also publishes 'relative' (the same change as a quotient) and 'absolute_change' (a change from baseline in the metric's unit, which for a ratio is points), because '+2 on ctr' is otherwise ambiguous." .

xeo:targetValue a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:MetricTarget ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    dct:description "The value the metric should reach, interpreted per targetKind. Bounded per metric and kind at the edge — a percentage, a count, a rank and a currency do not share a range. In the Metric's unit, a ratio as a 0 to 1 quotient; a currency target also states targetCurrency." .

xeo:baseline a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:MetricTarget ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "observation" ;
    dct:description "The metric's value when the target was set — the anchor 'how far beyond target' is measured from. An observation captured onto an interpretation; baselineCapturedAt says when, because it is not the same instant as the target's creation. The cached value of baselineReading, which carries the window, scope and source a bare number cannot." .

xeo:baselineCapturedAt a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:MetricTarget ; rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "observation" .

xeo:isPrimary a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:MetricTarget ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    dct:description "Exactly one target per objective. The one the agent optimises for." .

xeo:deletedAt a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "Soft-delete stamp. XEO never destroys a node something else was derived from — xeo-decision states the rule for a Practice (destroying it destroys the record of what it vetoed) and it holds here for a Project, a Campaign, or a MetricTarget that measured history hangs off. Absent on a live node; domain left open so any revisable term can carry it." .

# --- v0.6.0 (kit sync) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Appended at the foot, so no line above moves.
#
# ADDED. The agency relations between Organizations: who is whose client, and
# what a team is able to do. Organization itself, with owns and
# organizationKind, is declared in xeo-core.ttl (moved there 2026-11-12, before
# release): it is the canonical organization, not a delivery term. These two
# edges stay here because they are agency and scope terms.

xeo:clientOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "client of" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Organization ; rdfs:range xeo:Organization ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "This Organization is served by that one: a brand is the client of an agency. The contract itself is a Project on the client's Website; this edge says only who works for whom." .

xeo:holdsCapability a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "holds capability" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Organization ; rdfs:range xeo:Capability ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "entity" ;
    dct:description "A Capability this Organization is able to bring: the lever exists in this team. A third question beside the two the scope gate already asks. holdsCapability says the party can do it; approved says the lever is cleared for this engagement; inScope says the contract covers it." .

# --- v0.6.0 annotation completeness -----------------------------------------------
# The triples below add what the declarations above lacked; nothing is redefined.

xeo:hasCampaign dct:description "A campaign run under this Project." .

xeo:baselineCapturedAt dct:description "When baseline was read. Not the same instant as the target's creation." .

xeo:inScope xeo:rangeIncludes xeo:Intervention , xeo:Tactic .

# Labels for the properties declared above, which carried none.

xeo:hasProject rdfs:label "has project" .
xeo:hasCampaign rdfs:label "has campaign" .
xeo:inScope rdfs:label "in scope" .
xeo:aboutTopic rdfs:label "about topic" .
xeo:coversUrl rdfs:label "covers URL" .
xeo:coversTerm rdfs:label "covers term" .
xeo:hasObjective rdfs:label "has objective" .
xeo:hasTarget rdfs:label "has target" .
xeo:issuedFor rdfs:label "issued for" .
xeo:measures rdfs:label "measures" .
xeo:effortEstimate rdfs:label "effort estimate" .
xeo:execution rdfs:label "execution" .
xeo:engagementType rdfs:label "engagement type" .
xeo:interventionQuota rdfs:label "intervention quota" .
xeo:cadence rdfs:label "cadence" .
xeo:durationDays rdfs:label "duration days" .
xeo:resultsWindowDays rdfs:label "results window days" .


xeo:targetKind rdfs:label "target kind" .
xeo:targetValue rdfs:label "target value" .
xeo:baseline rdfs:label "baseline" .
xeo:baselineCapturedAt rdfs:label "baseline captured at" .
xeo:isPrimary rdfs:label "is primary" .
xeo:deletedAt rdfs:label "deleted at" .

# --- v0.6.0 (metrics and CRM pipeline, 2026-11-10) --------------------------------
# Appended at the foot, so no line above moves. From the two research reports.
#
# ADDED. baselineReading, the reading behind a target's cached baseline;
# resultsWindowStart, because a window length with no start cannot be computed;
# targetCurrency, because a currency target without a currency cannot be
# either; and objectiveReading (extension), the one reading an Objective is
# judged on.
#
# xeo:metric STAYS A STRING. The report asks for an object property to a
# Metric. Consumers store the code, so the property keeps its type and its
# meaning is tightened instead: the code is the skos:notation of a Metric in
# xeos:metric, the same "concept stored as its code" reading v0.6.0 gives
# sentiment, device and linkPosition. Nothing a consumer stores changes.
#
# DEPRECATED (advisory). xeo:direction. Its own description said it is derived
# from the metric; the Metric now states it once, as betterDirection. The term
# stays declared and valid, and a stored copy is still read.
#
# FIXED (layer). xeo:measures was marked observation. It records the design of
# an experiment, fixed when the experiment is set up, and is an episode.
#
# TIGHTENED (in place, above). The descriptions of Objective, MetricTarget,
# resultsWindowDays, metric, direction, targetKind, targetValue and baseline,
# one line each.

xeo:baselineReading a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "baseline reading" ;
    rdfs:range xeo:MetricReading ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "observation" ;
    xeo:groundedIn "The API contract of the system named in the reading's source" ;
    xeo:canonicalStore "neo4j" ;
    xeo:domainIncludes xeo:MetricTarget , xeo:Outcome ;
    dct:description "The reading a change is measured from. On a MetricTarget: the reading of its Metric taken when the target was set, of which xeo:baseline is the cached value. On an Outcome: the reading over the window of equal length immediately before the change was applied. One per subject. It carries what a bare number cannot: the window, the scope and the source, so the comparison can be recomputed. Domain left open across the two terms listed." .

xeo:resultsWindowStart a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "results window start" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Objective ; rdfs:range xsd:date ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    xeo:canonicalStore "neo4j" ;
    dct:description "The first day of the window an Objective's targets are read over. The window runs for resultsWindowDays from this day, which is counted. One per Objective. Without it resultsWindowDays is a length with nowhere to start." .

xeo:targetCurrency a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "target currency" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:MetricTarget ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    xeo:canonicalStore "neo4j" ;
    dct:description "The ISO 4217 code (three upper-case letters) a currency target is expressed in. Required when the target's Metric has unit currency and is read from deal amounts (pipeline_created, revenue_won); amounts in other currencies are converted before they are compared, and the conversion is a derivation. Absent on any other target." .

xeo:objectiveReading a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "objective reading" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:Objective ; rdfs:range xeo:MetricReading ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "derivation" ;
    xeo:canonicalStore "neo4j" ;
    xeo:termStatus "extension" ;
    dct:description "The reading an Objective is judged on, one per target: the target's Metric over the deduplicated union of the campaign's coversUrl and coversTerm, across the results window, computed from the column store. Which target a reading belongs to is read from readingOf. The objective-level result is this reading against the target's baselineReading. It is never the sum of the campaign's Outcomes: overlapping scopes would be counted twice, and a non-additive metric cannot be summed at all." .




xeo:baseline rdfs:seeAlso xeo:baselineReading .

xeo:isPrimary skos:altLabel "KPI" ;
    skos:scopeNote "What practitioners call the KPI. XEO has no KPI class: no system surveyed models one as a type, and the role is this flag on a target." .

# --- v0.7.0 (grounding, 2026-11-12) ---------------------------------------------
# Appended at the foot, so no line above moves. Every observation names what it
# is grounded in; these 2 did not. Nothing else about them changes.

xeo:baseline xeo:groundedIn "The API contract of the system named in the source of the target's baselineReading" .
xeo:baselineCapturedAt xeo:groundedIn "The API contract of the system named in the source of the target's baselineReading" .

# --- v0.7.0 (target to Metric, 2026-11-12) ---------------------------------------------
# C5: a target links to its Metric node. The text code (metric) is removed.

xeo:targetMetric a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "target metric" ;
    rdfs:domain xeo:MetricTarget ; rdfs:range xeo:Metric ;
    xeo:xeoLayer "interpretation" ;
    dct:description "The Metric a MetricTarget is set on: a link to the Metric node (xeos:metric-ctr, xeos:metric-pipeline_created, or a Metric of your own). Exactly one per MetricTarget. Its type, unit, better direction and additivity are the Metric's. Replaces the text code metric (0.7)." .
